BioInform2 Technical Guide
Introduction

BioInform2 is a modular bioinformatics pipeline designed to process Next Generation Sequencing data using a workflow orchestration system.

The project demonstrates how modern genomics pipelines are structured using reusable workflow components and automated data processing.

The pipeline is implemented using the workflow engine Nextflow.

Pipeline Architecture

The BioInform2 pipeline processes sequencing data through several stages.

Pipeline flow:

FASTQ Input
      │
      ▼
Quality Control
      │
      ▼
Reference Genome Indexing
      │
      ▼
Sequence Alignment
      │
      ▼
SAM Output
Nextflow Workflow System

Nextflow is a workflow orchestration system designed for scalable scientific pipelines.

Instead of executing commands sequentially in a script, workflows are defined as independent processes connected through data flow.

Advantages:

reproducible pipelines

automatic parallel execution

modular pipeline design

easy integration with HPC or cloud systems

Workflow Modules

The pipeline consists of three modules.

FASTQC Module

This module performs sequencing quality control.

Tool used: FastQC

Purpose:

detect sequencing errors

measure base quality

detect contamination

analyze GC content

Input:

FASTQ sequencing reads

Output:

FastQC HTML quality report

BWA Index Module

This module prepares the reference genome for alignment.

Tool used: BWA

Command:

bwa index reference.fa

Indexing builds internal lookup structures that allow rapid alignment of DNA sequences.

Output:

Reference genome index files.

BWA Alignment Module

This module aligns sequencing reads to the reference genome.

Command used:

bwa mem reference.fa sample.fastq > aligned.sam

The output is a SAM file containing alignment information.

SAM files contain:

read identifier

mapping location

alignment score

sequence data

Nextflow Process Structure

Each Nextflow process defines three main sections:

Input
Output
Script

Example process:

process FASTQC {

 input:
 path reads

 output:
 path "*.html"

 script:
 """
 fastqc $reads
 """
}

This design makes workflows modular and reusable.

Engineering Concepts Demonstrated

The BioInform2 project demonstrates key engineering practices used in bioinformatics pipelines:

modular workflow design

reproducible research pipelines

automation of genomics analysis

scientific data processing

Linux-based computational biology workflows

